ptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "author_association": "MEMBER", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "draft": false, "pull_request": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/uv/pulls/21966", "html_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/21966", "diff_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/21966.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/21966.patch", "merged_at": "2026-09-25T12:33:47Z"}, "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nSee https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/21963#issuecomment-5812891907 for context.\r\n\r\nTL;DR: our previous digest benchmarks were benching a single function call at a time, which is was too noisy. We now run the benchmark as batches of 500 calls at a time.\r\n\r\n<!-- What's the purpose of the change? What does it do, and why? -->\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\nNFC, benching only.\r\n\r\n<!-- How was it tested? -->\r\n", "closed_by": {"login": "woodruffw", "id": 3059210, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjMwNTkyMTA=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3059210?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw", "html_url": "https://github.com/woodruffw", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/uv/issues/21966/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/uv/issues/21966/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null}, "repos/astral-sh/uv/issues/21966/comments?per_page=100&page=1": [{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/uv/issues/comments/5817689135", "html_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/21966#issuecomment-5817689135", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/uv/issues/21966", "id": 5817689135, "node_id": "IC_kwDOKbIFZc8AAAABWsLkLw", "user": {"login": "woodruffw", "id": 3059210, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjMwNTkyMTA=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3059210?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw", "html_url": "https://github.com/woodruffw", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-09-24T16:05:17Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T16:05:17Z", "body": "Just leaving some notes here:\r\n\r\nI dug a bit into https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/21963#issuecomment-5812891907 and why it showed a performance improvement on the digest microbenchmarks. The TL;DR is that it's a combination of two things:\r\n\r\n1. The PR changes the binary layout such that `str::from_utf8` now sits at the head of an instruction cache line rather than halfway through one, meaning that it went from touching 5 cache lines to four. \r\n2. Our microbenchmarks are run in simulation mode, including simulated cache line performance. And CodSpeed clears the simulated caches before each measurement, so we essentially paid the cold-cache cost on each run, meaning that our runtime was overly influenced by cache behavior rather than the actual instruction cost.\r\n\r\nThese single-call benchmarks were unusually sensitive to the simulated cold-cache footprint of the binary. That allowed unrelated layout changes to produce substantial score changes even though the executed instructions were unchanged. Batching calls amortizes the initial cache-fill cost and makes the benchmark more representative of repeated execution with warm caches. It still includes instruction and memory-access costs, including any cache misses that occur during the batch.\r\n\r\n(There's still a fundamental question here that applies to all microbenchmarks, i.e. whether they're truly representative. In this case they almost certainly aren't since real execution in uv will have different I$/D$ behavior. But at least this will make the microbenchmarks consistent/not influenced by larger binary layout changes.)", "author_association": "MEMBER", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/uv/issues/comments/5817689135/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/uv/issues/comments/5818021650", "html_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/21966#issuecomment-5818021650", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/uv/issues/21966", "id": 5818021650, "node_id": "IC_kwDOKbIFZc8AAAABWsf3Eg", "user": {"login": "woodruffw", "id": 3059210, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjMwNTkyMTA=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3059210?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw", "html_url": "https://github.com/woodruffw", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2026-09-24T16:26:36Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T16:27:23Z", "body": "And for more context: an alternative here would be to switch from simulated to walltime for microbenchmarks. But that also runs the risk of being noisy (per https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/20165) and more generally might also mask interesting results (since the noise floor will go up, making it harder to detect positive/negative changes in a microbenchmarking setting).\r\n\r\nHowever also per https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/20165 we probably want to make it harder for us to _accidentally_ bucket a benchmark as simultation or walltime-only, since it makes it harder to make an empirical decision here.", "author_association": "MEMBER", "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/uv/issues/comments/5818021650/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}], "repos/astral-sh/uv/pulls/21966": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/uv/pulls/21966", "id": 4627331686, "node_id": "PR_kwDOKbIFZc8AAAABE896Zg", "html_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/21966", "diff_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/21966.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/21966.patch", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/astral-sh/uv/issues/21966", "number": 21966, "state": "closed", "locked": false, "title": "bench: attempt to stabilize digest benchmarks", "user": {"login": "woodruffw", "id": 3059210, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjMwNTkyMTA=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3059210?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw", "html_url": "https://github.com/woodruffw", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/woodruffw/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nSee https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/21963#issuecomment-5812891907 for context.\r\n\r\nTL;DR: our previous digest benchmarks were benching a single function call at a time, which is was too noisy. We now run the benchmark as batches of 500 cal